    {
      "id": "gv-793469-b00001",
      "text": "From Barbie tacos to Barbie planes, Latin America has jumped on the Barbie bandwagon. The film, directed by Greta Gerwig and starring Margot Robbie and Ryan Gosling, ranked third in Mexico in the movie's box office performance worldwide on its opening weekend. Brazil came right after and Argentina was also in the top countries.",
      "page": null,
      "paragraph": 1,
      "body_start": 0,
      "body_end": 329,
      "source_links": [
        "https://es.statista.com/estadisticas/1401700/taquilla-de-barbie-durante-su-fin-de-semana-de-estreno-por-pais/"
      ],
      "source_kind": "p",
      "source_is_quotation": false
    },
    {
      "id": "gv-793469-b00002",
      "text": "Californian actress of Honduran descent, América Ferreran also starred in Barbie and now has a Barbie doll modeled after her. She stated to Collider that “[t]he fact that there’s a Barbie movie and that the story has shifted and expanded to include more of us to be able to be seen in that iconic and very culturally dominant brand, that’s very unexpected and not something that I ever thought I would say that I was a part of.”",
      "page": null,
      "paragraph": 2,
      "body_start": 331,
      "body_end": 759,
      "source_links": [
        "https://collider.com/barbie-america-ferrera-interview/",
        "https://www.parati.com.ar/news/asi-luce-la-muneca-inspirada-en-america-ferrera-la-actriz-hondurena-de-barbie/"
      ],
      "source_kind": "p",
      "source_is_quotation": false
    },
    {
      "id": "gv-793469-b00003",
      "text": "The overall marketing budget for Barbie's film and merchandise allegedly surpassed the film's own budget at $150 million. And in Latin America, street vendors, corporations, presidential candidates, and political activists are surfing the Barbie wave.",
      "page": null,
      "paragraph": 3,
      "body_start": 761,
      "body_end": 1012,
      "source_links": [
        "https://www.insider.com/barbie-had-150-million-marketing-budget-2023-7",
        "https://www.tiktok.com/@sandratorresgua/video/7258310588168703237?q=sandra%20torres%20barbie&t=1690456329534"
      ],
      "source_kind": "p",
      "source_is_quotation": false
    },
    {
      "id": "gv-793469-b00004",
      "text": "Barbie in food",
      "page": null,
      "paragraph": 4,
      "body_start": 1014,
      "body_end": 1028,
      "source_links": [],
      "source_kind": "h3",
      "source_is_quotation": false
    },
    {
      "id": "gv-793469-b00005",
      "text": "From Mexico to Chile, all kinds of corn doughs have been colored pink with beet juice or artificial coloring. Mexican and Guatemalan street vendors have attracted clients with pink tacos. Salvadoran, Venezuelan, and Chilean vendors have done the same with pupusas and arepas.",
      "page": null,
      "paragraph": 5,
      "body_start": 1030,
      "body_end": 1305,
      "source_links": [
        "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Arepa",
        "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pupusa",
        "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Taco"
      ],
      "source_kind": "p",
      "source_is_quotation": false
    },
    {
      "id": "gv-793469-b00006",
      "text": "Here is an example of the ‘Barbie tacos’, served in Guatemala City:",
      "page": null,
      "paragraph": 6,
      "body_start": 1307,
      "body_end": 1374,
      "source_links": [],
      "source_kind": "p",
      "source_is_quotation": false
    },
